---
// Worktrees: several agents on several branches of one repository, shown the
// way the app shows it: branch marks in the sidebar, the graph in History.
import Sidebar from '../../app/gen/Sidebar.astro';
import TerminalNarrow from '../../app/gen/TerminalNarrow.astro';
import History from '../../app/gen/History.astro';
---
<section class="sec" id="worktrees">
  <div class="page">
    <div class="bhead" data-reveal>
      <h2 class="h2">Five agents, one repository. <span class="tone">Open a session on a branch and Wortel checks it out in a directory of its own. Each agent edits its own files, and nothing changes the ground under another mid-task.</span></h2>
    </div>
    <div class="shot crop" style="--at: 82% 72%" aria-hidden="true">
      <div class="win wapp" inert>
        <div class="absolute inset-0 bg-sidebar backdrop-blur-[50px] backdrop-saturate-[1.8]"></div>
        <div class="relative flex size-full">
          <div class="flex w-[234px] shrink-0"><Sidebar /></div>
          <div class="w-px shrink-0 bg-sidebar-border"></div>
          <div class="flex min-w-[80px] flex-1"><TerminalNarrow /></div>
          <div class="w-px shrink-0 bg-sidebar-border"></div>
          <div class="flex w-[384px] min-w-[260px] shrink-[3]"><History /></div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
    <ul class="facts" data-reveal-group>
      <li class="fact" data-reveal>
        <h3 class="h3">A worktree per session <kbd>⇧⌘N</kbd></h3>
        <p class="body">It shares the repository’s history, objects and remotes, so it costs a directory, not a clone. A branch that has a worktree opens the one it has.</p>
      </li>
      <li class="fact" data-reveal>
        <h3 class="h3">Forks from the default branch</h3>
        <p class="body">Not from whichever agent’s half-finished branch you happened to be standing in.</p>
      </li>
      <li class="fact" data-reveal>
        <h3 class="h3">Out of the repository</h3>
        <p class="body">Worktrees live outside it, where they cannot be committed by accident, and each one’s inspector shows only its own work.</p>
      </li>
    </ul>
  </div>
</section>
